{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"peaceful-colourific-copepod","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe plan-review gate re-reviews a ticket's plan on entry into `in_progress`, including\nEXECUTION-phase re-reviews (a claimed ticket re-reviewed before close). At execution time a\nPass-1 finder can flag a plan-vs-code discrepancy that is actually the *expected* result of the\nplan's own directed work already having been done: the plan directs \"remove X\", the agent\nremoved X, and the re-review flags \"the plan references X but no symbol X exists\". During a\nPLANNING review that is a legitimate true positive; during an EXECUTION review it is a false\npositive that can block a correct, completed ticket from closing. Pass-2 has no way to drop it.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a single-answer Pass-2 VETO, mirroring the existing a8e5 absence-refuted veto, that drops\nsuch a finding only during an execution-phase review. A new plan-review-only binary sub-answer\n`current_state_satisfies_plan_goal` (na-default, OUTSIDE `GRADED_BINARY` so it never affects\nvalidity arithmetic) is set by the verifier via a present-state check: does the code AS IT IS\nNOW already satisfy the plan's directed end state? `pass3_decide` drops the finding\n(`reason=\"veto:plan-goal-satisfied\"`) only when a new keyword-only `execution_review` flag is\nTrue AND the answer is a definite `yes`. The flag is threaded from the existing\n`decide_ops` phase signal through `orchestrator.pass3_over_findings` into the kernel; it defaults\nFalse, so planning reviews and every code-review call are byte-unchanged. This is the least\nmechanism that resolves the planning-vs-execution asymmetry without new history/intent inference.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify_models.py` — add the na-default binary to the\n  plan-review-only `binary_extra_fields`.\n- `src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py` — add `execution_review` kwarg to `pass3_decide` +\n  `pass3_over_findings`; add the veto branch.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py` — thread `execution_review` into the kernel call.\n- `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_verifier.md`,\n  `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_verifier_agentic.md` — document the sub-answer.\n- `tests/unit/test_review_kernel.py`, `tests/unit/test_plan_review.py` — tests.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: `execution_review=True` + `current_state_satisfies_plan_goal=\"yes\"` at full\n  validity/impact ⇒ dropped with `reason=\"veto:plan-goal-satisfied\"`.\n- Edge (planning preserved): same finding with `execution_review=False` ⇒ NOT dropped.\n- Edge (definite-yes only): `no`/`insufficient`/`na`/absent under execution ⇒ NOT dropped.\n- Contract: the plan-review verification model carries the field, it is na-default, and it is\n  absent from `GRADED_BINARY` and from the base/code-review models.\n- Integration: `orchestrator.pass3_over_findings` threads the phase flag (planning keeps,\n  execution drops).\n- RED/GREEN verified against the source diff; the decide veto branch is mutation-tested.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A Pass-2 finding with `current_state_satisfies_plan_goal=\"yes\"` is dropped with\n  `reason=\"veto:plan-goal-satisfied\"` when `pass3_decide` is called with `execution_review=True`,\n  even at validity 1.0 and impact 1.0.\n- [ ] The same finding is NOT dropped when `execution_review=False` (planning-phase true\n  positive preserved).\n- [ ] Under `execution_review=True`, answers `no`, `insufficient`, `na`, and an absent key do\n  NOT drop the finding.\n- [ ] `current_state_satisfies_plan_goal` is present on the plan-review verification model,\n  defaults to `\"na\"`, and is NOT a member of `GRADED_BINARY` (so validity is unchanged); the\n  base and code-review models do not carry it.\n- [ ] `orchestrator.pass3_over_findings(..., execution_review=True)` drops the finding while\n  `execution_review=False` keeps it, proving the phase flag is threaded end to end.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass.","id":"c46b-a2e8-25e8-4059","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Execution-phase Pass-2 on-target veto for completed-work false positives"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786148871077344001,"uuid":"5cee22f8-a922-4913-b1df-b7d390797426"}